cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Geyser Genomics, please cite it as below, and cite the tools and
  data it builds on (listed under references).
title: "Geyser Genomics: an event-driven AWS pipeline from FASTQ to VCF"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shaw
    given-names: Harry
repository-code: "https://github.com/Harry5haw/Geyser-Genomics"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An event-driven pipeline on AWS (S3, Lambda, Step Functions, Batch, all in
  Terraform) that turns a gzipped FASTQ into a VCF, developed offline first
  against synthetic data with planted mutations, with linear and
  pangenome-aware DeepVariant benchmarked against bcftools with hap.py.
keywords:
  - genomics
  - bioinformatics
  - variant calling
  - pangenome
  - deepvariant
  - aws
  - terraform
